WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.007
TIMESTAMP stores a date and local clock time.

00:00:03.007 --> 00:00:06.267
It does not carry a time-zone interpretation.

00:00:06.267 --> 00:00:10.427
That can be appropriate when the time zone is fixed or irrelevant.

00:00:10.427 --> 00:00:15.127
But if records come from multiple regions or you need to compare global instants,

00:00:15.127 --> 00:00:18.007
a plain timestamp can become ambiguous.

00:00:18.007 --> 00:00:20.717
Choose temporal types based on meaning.

00:00:20.717 --> 00:00:24.057
DATE is for calendar dates without time of day.

00:00:24.057 --> 00:00:28.447
TIMESTAMP stores a date and time without a time-zone interpretation.

00:00:28.447 --> 00:00:34.682
TIMESTAMPTZ represents an instant in time and is usually safer for events that cross regions or

00:00:34.682 --> 00:00:36.376
daylight-saving changes.
